package toolruntime

// Diagnostic claims need evidence appropriate to that claim, independently of
// whether the query execution and numerical calculation succeeded.
const DiagnosticClaimInstructions = ` Keep requested time bounds separate from actual returned first/last sample timestamps. Existing offline evidence helpers provide evaluation_window facts: use their signed offsets and before/equal/after relations for time comparisons, rather than mentally recomputing elapsed minutes or reversing endpoint order. Positive offsets mean after; negative offsets mean before. A returned endpoint span is not raw sampling coverage or ingestion completeness. When those facts are unavailable, omit the precise elapsed-time claim. Derive any claimed extrema position and UTC timestamp from the original timestamp-value pairs with code; never substitute the request start, first value or minimum for a maximum's position. If those facts were not computed, omit that precise claim. Briefly qualify limited sample coverage. Low utilization alone does not establish overall health or absence of anomalies without a relevant threshold, baseline or alert assessment. Network IO alone does not establish packet drops/errors, network topology, mirrored paths or causal relationships, even when series look similar; state unqueried signals as unknown. Do not attribute missing evaluation points to extrapolation, engine behavior or collection causes unless that reason is verified. Prefer the existing computed evidence cards/report and a brief supported business summary; do not add speculative health explanations to fill the answer.`
